  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Johnny Carson was an American television host and comedian whose three decades presenting The Tonight Show made him a central figure in late-night entertainment. His highly paid broadcasting career and television production business created substantial wealth. His programme introduced generations of comedians to national audiences, and he received the Presidential Medal of Freedom.",
    "html": "<p>Johnny Carson was an American television host and comedian whose three decades presenting The Tonight Show made him a central figure in late-night entertainment. His highly paid broadcasting career and television production business created substantial wealth. His programme introduced generations of comedians to national audiences, and he received the Presidential Medal of Freedom.</p>\r\n",
